// WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM extdeps.memory.samsung (DESIGN 3).
// Cisco resells a Samsung module under its own PID and part number, with its own lifecycle and
// its own published description. That is a second independently governed entity inhabiting the
// same shape, not a second name for the Samsung row -- so it gets its own module authority and
// REFERENCES the module rather than restating its organization axes. A second OEM reselling the
// same part would be another row here and no edit to Samsung at all.
//
// CITATION STANDING, STATED HONESTLY BECAUSE IT IS WEAKER THAN THE ANCHOR SUGGESTS.
// The anchor above is Cisco's C-Series datasheet index, not a document carrying this PID. The
// per-PID spec sheets under cisco.com/c/dam refuse automated retrieval (HTTP 403, checked
// 2026-08-22), and the M4-era memory guide that would carry a 2133 TSV-RDIMM was not reachable.
// What established the description below was agreement across independent distributor listings
// -- 64 GB, DDR4-2133 / PC4-17000, TSV-RDIMM, octal rank, x4, 1.2 V, CL15 -- corroborated by the
// operator's physical label. That is a real basis and it is NOT a first-party reading, which is
// exactly the distinction OemModuleLinkEvidence's two arms exist to keep visible.
// Dissolve-on: a reachable Cisco memory guide or spec sheet listing this PID, at which point the
// anchor names that document and this paragraph shrinks to a citation.
//
// WHAT THE LABEL SETTLED THAT NOTHING ELSE COULD. The label reads
// "M393A8G40D40-CRB0Q S", which is what links this Cisco PID to that specific Samsung part
// number -- no reachable Cisco document names the underlying manufacturer part at all. The link
// is therefore an observation of the part in hand, recorded as such.
data ucs_mr_1x648ru_a: extdeps.memory.types.OemModuleOffering = extdeps.memory.types.OemModuleOffering {
  oem: extdeps.vendor.cisco.cisco,
  oem_product_id: "UCS-MR-1X648RU-A",
  oem_part_number: "15-102952-01",
  underlying_module: extdeps.memory.samsung.m393a8g40d40_crb0q_catalog,
  link_evidence: extdeps.memory.types.OemLinkPhysicalLabelObserved {
    label_text: "M393A8G40D40-CRB0Q S",
    observer: "operator, physical label on the module in hand, 2026-08-22",
  },
}
